training-agents-into-weights-lines-12 : List (List Word)
training-agents-into-weights-lines-12 = cons "- **The corpus is my own words.** Months of messages, essays written hourly, carry argument and" (cons "  conclusion together. A training example is a whole message: cutting a message to a length limit" (cons "  separates a conclusion from the argument establishing it." (cons "- **The supervision is already done.** Every agent message in my transcripts is followed by my" (cons "  reply: accepted, corrected, or rejected with the reason. Those replies label tens of thousands of" (cons "  turns. A model of my reaction to an agent message, trained on them, grades new agent output" (cons "  without me in the loop." (cons "- **Rejected samples come from the model being trained.** An open model's defaults differ from" (cons "  Claude's; it is placed in the project's situations, and its own contrary decisions are the" (cons "  rejected side of each pair, graded against the project's rules and the paper. A frontier model given the" (cons "  whole context still made contrary decisions, so a model's taste is not the grader." (cons "- **Continuous training is a maintained view.** Each training example is keyed by the content of the" (cons "  objects it came from; new interaction, correction and writing enters the corpus as new objects," (cons "  and only what depends on changed objects is regenerated (docs/hyperactivity_v31.pdf, 14 Nov 2026," (cons (quoted (cons "  sha256 9c480995e7fb…, §10.2 " (cons "A maintained view is a proof about an update" (cons " and §10.5 " (cons "Dependency" nil))))) (cons (quoted (cons "  certificates and persistent evaluation" (cons "). The trained adapter is one more content-addressed object," nil))) (cons "  its dependencies the corpus it was trained on." (cons "- **The checker for the mathematics.** The machine's `--serve` answers declarations with acceptance" (cons "  or failure, so constructions of the paper and the task graph are reinforcement-learning tasks" (cons "  rewarded on the first submission only." (cons "" nil))))))))))))))))))))
